  "body": "[Character reference state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#character-reference-state) has switch for consumed character. In `Anything else` case spec tells to:\r\n\r\n> Consume the maximum number of characters possible, with the consumed characters matching one of the identifiers in the first column of the named character references table (in a case-sensitive manner)\r\n\r\nIt's not clear from the spec if match should include character for which switch was performed (SPOILER: it should) or start consuming and matching characters after it.\r\n\r\nI suggest to introduce `Named character reference state` and just reconsume in it in `Anything else` case to get rid of ambiguity.\r\n\r\nI'll issue a PR if everyone is OK with this change. \\cc @RReverser @zcorpan ",
